<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE topic
        SYSTEM "https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/xhtml-entities.dtd">
<topic xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
       xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/topic.v2.xsd"
       title="JirAI: Install" id="JirAI-Installation">

    <primary-label ref="jirai"/>
    <show-structure for="chapter,procedure" depth="2"/>

    <tldr>
        <p>Install: <ui-path>Settings | Plugins | Marketplace</ui-path>, search for JirAI</p>
        <p>Requires: a JetBrains IDE 2026.3 or later and a Jira Cloud site</p>
        <p>Price: free</p>
    </tldr>

    <link-summary>Check the requirements and install JirAI from JetBrains Marketplace, in the IDE, from the website or from disk.</link-summary>
    <card-summary>Check the requirements and install the free JirAI plugin.</card-summary>
    <web-summary>Install the free JirAI plugin for Jira Cloud in IntelliJ IDEA and other JetBrains IDEs from JetBrains Marketplace, and check the requirements.</web-summary>

    <p>Install JirAI from JetBrains Marketplace, restart the IDE and sign in to your Jira Cloud site.</p>
    <p>JirAI is free: you need no license, trial or subscription to install and use it.</p>

    <chapter title="Requirements" id="requirements">
        <list>
            <li><p>The current version requires a JetBrains IDE 2026.3 (build 263) or later.</p></li>
            <li>
                <p>A Jira Cloud site, for example <code>https://demo-org.atlassian.net</code>.</p>
                <p>Jira Server and Jira Data Center are not supported.</p>
            </li>
            <li><p>An Atlassian account with access to the site, and an API token for that account.</p></li>
            <li>
                <p>Optional: the bundled Git plugin and a Git repository in the project.</p>
                <p>They are needed only to create branches from issues, show the current issue in the status bar and start commit messages with the issue key.</p>
                <p>If you disable the Git plugin, only these features stop working.</p>
            </li>
        </list>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Install JirAI" id="install-methods">
        <tabs>
            <tab title="In the IDE" id="install-ide">
                <procedure title="Install JirAI from the IDE" id="install-from-ide-proc">
                    <step><p>Open the <control>Settings</control> dialog: <shortcut>Ctrl+Alt+S</shortcut> (macOS: <shortcut>⌘ ,</shortcut>).</p></step>
                    <step><p>Select <control>Plugins</control>.</p></step>
                    <step><p>Open the <control>Marketplace</control> tab.</p></step>
                    <step><p>Search for JirAI.</p></step>
                    <step><p>Click <control>Install</control>.</p></step>
                    <step><p>Restart the IDE when prompted.</p></step>
                </procedure>
            </tab>
            <tab title="From the Marketplace website" id="install-web">
                <procedure title="Install JirAI from the website" id="install-from-web-proc">
                    <step><p>Open the <a href="https://plugins.jetbrains.com/plugin/33954-jirai">JirAI page on JetBrains Marketplace</a>.</p></step>
                    <step><p>Click <control>Install to…</control> and choose the running IDE.</p></step>
                    <step><p>In the IDE, confirm the installation.</p></step>
                    <step><p>Restart the IDE when prompted.</p></step>
                </procedure>
            </tab>
            <tab title="From disk" id="install-disk">
                <procedure title="Install JirAI from a ZIP archive" id="install-from-disk-proc">
                    <step><p>Download the plugin ZIP archive from the <a href="https://plugins.jetbrains.com/plugin/33954-jirai/versions">JirAI versions page</a>.</p></step>
                    <step><p>In <ui-path>Settings | Plugins</ui-path>, click the gear icon.</p></step>
                    <step><p>Choose <control>Install Plugin from Disk…</control>.</p></step>
                    <step><p>Select the ZIP archive.</p></step>
                    <step><p>Restart the IDE when prompted.</p></step>
                </procedure>
                <note>
                    <p>Under Remote Development, the IDE synchronizes only plugins that come from JetBrains Marketplace or a custom repository.</p>
                    <p>A plugin installed from disk must be installed on the host and on the client separately.</p>
                </note>
            </tab>
        </tabs>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="After installation" id="next-steps">
        <p>Open the <control>JirAI</control> tool window and sign in to your Jira Cloud site, as described in <a href="JirAI-Sign-In-and-Configuration.topic">Sign in and manage your account</a>.</p>
    </chapter>

